{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"title":"MXLPedal.Kind","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPedalV4KindO","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The change, continue, discontinue, and resume types are used when the line attribute is yes. The change type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates a pedal lift and retake indicated with an inverted V marking. The continue type allows more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precise formatting across system breaks and for more complex pedaling lines. The discontinue type indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the end of a pedal line that does not include the explicit lift represented by the stop type. The resume","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type indicates the start of a pedal line that does not include the downstroke represented by the start","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type. It can be used when a line resumes after being discontinued, or to start a pedal line that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preceded by a text or symbol representation of the pedal.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal-type simple type is used to distinguish types of pedal directions. The start value indicates the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a damper pedal, while the sostenuto value indicates the start of a sostenuto pedal. The other values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be used with either the damper or sostenuto pedal. The soft pedal is not included here because there is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no special symbol or graphic used for it beyond what can be specified with words and bracket elements.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/change","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/continue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/discontinue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/resume","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/sostenuto","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/start","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/stop"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum/Equatable-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/Equatable-Implementations","kind":"article","title":"Equatable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/equatable-implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}],"title":"MXLPedal","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"typ